James sought help with the Schwab API, specifically regarding an OAuth error encountered during token retrieval, indicating issues with authorization code decryption. I provided troubleshooting suggestions, including verifying authorization code integrity, redirect URI matches, content-type headers, special character encoding, and server clock synchronization. James later reported issues with the `schwab-py` library, specifically an error occurring during the import of the `easy_client`, which triggered an immediate OAuth flow. I advised checking for the latest library version, ensuring proper client configuration, reviewing the library's implementation, and implementing error handling. Additionally, I suggested contacting library support and considering a manual OAuth implementation if issues persisted.
